AB  - In this study, two highly efficient PEFT techniques Soft Prompts and LoRA will be examined by applying them to DistilBERT pre-trained model. The effectiveness of the chosen fine-tuning techniques will be compared through conducting experiments with three different tasks in NLP domain – fake news classification, spam detection, and sentiment analysis on Amazon Fine Food Reviews data set. In order to make the comparison more accurate, six indicators will be taken into consideration during evaluations – accuracy, F1 score, precision, recall, training, and evaluation time. According to obtained results, the LoRA technique proves its superiority over other techniques in terms of efficiency as it yields the best results both in terms of metrics and time.
