AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable efficacy across diverse domains, yet their deployment in sensitive sectors is constrained by data privacy. Federated Learning (FL) offers a promising paradigm for collaborative model training without exposing raw data, while Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) techniques substantially reduce adaptation costs. This survey systematically reviews the integration of FL and PEFT for LLMs, elucidating foundational architectures, mainstream PEFT methodologies, and federated adaptation frameworks. We analyze representative approaches, highlight open challenges, including communication bottlenecks, task and model heterogeneity, parameter anonymity, and adaptation profile misalignment, and propose future research directions. Our work aims to provide a comprehensive reference for advancing privacy-preserving, scalable, and efficient LLM fine-tuning in federated environments.
