AB  - The growing complexity of decentralized power systems has the need for intelligent, adaptive tools to support real-time decision-making in microgrid operations. This paper introduces GridLLaMA, a domain-adapted large language model fine-tuned from LLaMA 3.1 (8B) to provide context-aware and precise technically responses across key operational domains Power quality, demand response, voltage stability, and renewable integration. A specialized question-answer (QA) dataset was constructed from 700 technical documents which include Research papers and IEEE standards. The model was fine-tuned using parameter-efficient LoRA methods and filtered through the Nemotron-4 reward model to ensure high-quality instructional responses. Evaluation against a benchmark of general and expert-level questions evaluated via blind review by domain experts demonstrated that GridLLaMA significantly outperforms the base model, achieving 94% accuracy on general questions and 78% on expert-level questions, compared to the base model's 6% and 22%, respectively. The results indicate the potential of domain-specific LLM adaptation for -focused applications and validate GridLLaMA as a scalable tool for intelligent microgrid management.
