AB  - In this study, a text classification system was developed to automatically classify Turkish user reviews based on their rating labels. Both encoder-based BERTurk models and decoder-based Gemma models were utilized, and parameter efficiency in large language models was achieved by applying the LoRA (Low-Rank Adaptation) method. The effectiveness of the models was examined with varying sizes of the training dataset. Gemma model achieved 69.80% accuracy and 65.56% F1 score with 10.000 training and 2.000 test samples. The same Gemma model achieved 59% accuracy and 55.45% F1 score with 1.000 training and 200 test samples. BERTurk model achieved 74.13% accuracy and 72.17% F1 score with 100.000 training and 20.000 test samples. Additionally, the BERTurk model achieved 66% accuracy and 54.87% F1 score on 1.000 training and 200 test samples. The results of the experiment indicate that model performance varies based on both model size and training data volume, and BERTurk and Gemma models perform well particularly on large datasets.
