AB  - Fake reviews influence consumer trust and purchasing decisions. The identification of fake reviews is thus important for online shops. Contrast with English where much work has been done there is limited work on fake reviews detection for Arabic. Wide-ranging datasets are currently not widely available. This paper presents the development and evaluation of several models to detect Arabic fake reviews. We optimize several linguistic models like LLaMA-v2 and ALLAM. We subsequently compare their results withBERT-based models, namely CamelBERT and MARBERT. The models received training and testing on the combination of real and synthetic reviews within the framework of Arabic datasets consisting of AFRD, as well as Arabic translated versions of respective Amazon and Yelp reviews datasets. For each tested methodology, the evaluation of the model was carried out using configurations comprising Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score. Our few-shot experiment in this paper for GPT-5.0, DeepSeek, and Gemini is done using five examples from each class. The goal is to test the expert models for generalization on respective datasets of Amazon, Yelp, and AFRD. The performance results for few-shot show an accuracy score of 74%, 64% and 35% on Amazon, Yelp and AFRD respectively along with P, R, F1 vales. The fine-tuned BERT models outperform all aforementioned LLMs on all datasets as per the experimental results.
