AB  - In the context of oil and gas exploration and development, constructing high-quality image-text datasets and enhancing model comprehension of professional geological illustrations have become an urgent need. To address the challenges of high data redundancy, excessive noise, scarce image-text features, and difficult semantic alignment, this paper proposes an Agent-driven multi-skill adaptive orchestration mechanism. By integrating specialized atomic capabilities (skills) such as cross-modal retrieval, noise filtering, and text refinement, the mechanism enables the automatic extraction and construction of 20,920 image-text pairs across 17 categories. LoRA fine-tuning experiments demonstrate that the constructed dataset improves model comprehension. Furthermore, a visual review platform is developed to support dataset quality auditing and subjective comparative evaluation of fine-tuning performance, providing a systematic solution for large-scale multimodal dataset construction in the oil and gas domain.
